ref='Failure testing declares expected outputs and forbidden operations before the run. Complete main matrix: malformed A with extra role field → invalid_input/null claims/no lookup; student T → denied/null/no lookup; absent Z → review/null/lookup Z; approved current A c1 → supported12/REG-A/lookup A. All four pass when response, claims and exact trace agree. Denial/review can be correct outcomes. Deliberate bad-order T trace contains lookup T before denial, so that case fails and only 3/4 pass in the separate counterexample. Preserve original failed trace and later regression evidence. Separate picture: current approved F4 says club time15:00, drafting unavailable, checked template explicitly allowed → supported “The club time is 15:00.”/F4 with degraded mode. If retrieval also fails, or evidence invalid/unapproved, review with null claim/source; template cannot invent evidence. Code uses local flags/dictionaries, no actual restricted reads, model calls or provider failures. Four main cases plus added probes are not every timeout/stale/interaction test. Mandatory gates remain independent of aggregate pass rates.'
